

On-disc data-structures
-----------------------

The PBAs 0-7 each contain a Superblock. The Tresor cycles through these PBAs
whenever it stores its current Superblock. When opening a Tresor container, the
current Superblock can be determined via its hash, that gets written to the
Trust Anchor after having written back the Superblock

 containing references to the VBD-Snapshots, the Free Tree,
and the Meta Tree.

A VBD tree configured by the user to have N levels looks as follows:

* Level #N+1: Root node (Part of a Superblock)
* Level #1..#N: Blocks of Type-1 nodes
* Level #0: User Data blocks

The depicted tree level indices are used 
